Inheritance:-
Need for Java Inheritance:-
1. Code reusability: The basic need of inheritance is to reuse the features. If you have defined the functionality once, by using inheritance, you can easily use it in other classes and packages.
2. Extensibility: The inheritance helps to extend the functionalities of a class. If you have a base class with some functionalities, you can extend them by using inheritance in the derived class.
3. Implantation of method overriding: Inheritance is required to achieve one of the concepts of Polymorphism, which is method overriding.
4. Achieve Abstraction: Another concept of OPPs that is Abstraction also needs Inheritance.

The Super Keyword:-
1. It is used to differentiate the members of the superclass from the members of the subclass, if they have the same name.
2. It is used to invoke the superclass constructor from a subclass.
